    board: file CF-144 — the closure-evidence rule conflates three tree_fp instruments
    
    QA lane code-factory-duckbrain-qa-2026-11-04-02-20-15.
    
    Census at d02916e over every complete row's detail.evidence entries: 4 declare
    a per-entry fingerprint_algo and hold the sha256 of the named artifact
    (CF-064, CF-065, CF-091, CF-092 — all recompute exactly), 5 hold a 40-hex git
    tree oid (CF-055 equals git rev-parse <commit>^{tree}), 37 hold a bare 64-hex
    value with no declared algorithm, 1 is empty. git cat-file -t answers
    "fatal: Not a valid object name" for all four declared digests, so the rule
    prescribed by CF-047 AC2 and gated by CF-074 AC1 ("tree_fp must resolve via
    git cat-file -t to a git tree") would fail the four closures that are honest
    and recomputable. scripts/boardctl validate accepts the field today.
    
